@startuml
title Relational Access - SQL Execution Lifecycle

hide empty description
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam linetype polyline
left to right direction

state CREATED
state VALIDATING
state RESOLVING_DATASOURCE
state ACQUIRING_CONNECTION
state PREPARING_STATEMENT
state BINDING_PARAMETERS
state EXECUTING
state MAPPING_RESULT
state BUILDING_RESULT
state TRANSLATING_EXCEPTION
state RELEASING_RESOURCES
state NOTIFYING_LISTENER
state SUCCEEDED
state TERMINATED_WITH_ERROR

[*] --> CREATED
CREATED --> VALIDATING : RelationalTemplate method called

VALIDATING --> RESOLVING_DATASOURCE : statement/options valid
VALIDATING --> RELEASING_RESOURCES : invalid request\n(no JDBC resources yet)

RESOLVING_DATASOURCE --> ACQUIRING_CONNECTION : DataSource resolved
RESOLVING_DATASOURCE --> TRANSLATING_EXCEPTION : resolution failure

ACQUIRING_CONNECTION --> PREPARING_STATEMENT : ConnectionHandle acquired
ACQUIRING_CONNECTION --> TRANSLATING_EXCEPTION : SQLException

PREPARING_STATEMENT --> BINDING_PARAMETERS : PreparedStatement created
PREPARING_STATEMENT --> TRANSLATING_EXCEPTION : SQLException

BINDING_PARAMETERS --> EXECUTING : parameters/options bound
BINDING_PARAMETERS --> TRANSLATING_EXCEPTION : SQLException

EXECUTING --> MAPPING_RESULT : query
EXECUTING --> BUILDING_RESULT : update / batch / generated-key
EXECUTING --> TRANSLATING_EXCEPTION : SQLException

MAPPING_RESULT --> BUILDING_RESULT : mapping complete
MAPPING_RESULT --> TRANSLATING_EXCEPTION : SQLException / mapping failure

BUILDING_RESULT --> RELEASING_RESOURCES : result ready
TRANSLATING_EXCEPTION --> RELEASING_RESOURCES : stable failure created

RELEASING_RESOURCES --> NOTIFYING_LISTENER : ResultSet / Statement / Handle released
NOTIFYING_LISTENER --> SUCCEEDED : no recorded failure
NOTIFYING_LISTENER --> TERMINATED_WITH_ERROR : recorded failure

SUCCEEDED --> [*]
TERMINATED_WITH_ERROR --> [*]

note bottom of TRANSLATING_EXCEPTION
SQLException is translated to
RelationalAccessException + RelationalFailureType.
Relational Access itself does NOT retry SQL.
end note

note bottom of RELEASING_RESOURCES
ConnectionHandle.close() follows ownership:
OWNED -> physical close
BORROWED -> logical release only
end note

@enduml
